ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS FOR THIS WORK

When sharing this work or derivative works publicly, attribution must include:

  - The original author: P. Steven Lorenz
  - A link to the original repository: https://github.com/pslorenz/security-policy-templates
  - The license: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  - An indication of any changes made

Attribution may be given once for a collection, for example in a README or a
NOTICE file distributed with it. It does not need to appear in each document.

Organizations adopting documents for their own internal use do not need to
credit the source in those documents. Each document carries a closing line
that says so, and that line may be removed. scripts/generate.py removes it by
default and writes a NOTICE file with the generated documents instead.

Anyone who redistributes the library, or a collection of documents derived
from it, to others (for example, a provider publishing a policy pack) must give
the credit described above.

